pirate-rev-salary-cut = Central Command cuts salaries for the { $department } department by { $percent }%. Total reduction: { $total }%.
pirate-rev-order-slimes = raising slimes is prohibited. Destroy all existing slimes. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 303 (Possession of Class A Contraband).
pirate-rev-order-music = music, including instruments, jukeboxes and singing, is prohibited. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 105 (Hooliganism).
pirate-rev-order-plushies = plush toys are prohibited. Surrender them to Security. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 303 (Possession of Class A Contraband).
pirate-rev-order-cash = cash credits are prohibited; use cashless payments. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 303 (Possession of Class A Contraband).
pirate-rev-order-gloves = gloves are prohibited except for Security; only the Chief Engineer may wear insulated gloves. Surrender gloves to Security and insulated gloves to the Chief Engineer. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 103 (Misuse of SCC Assets).
pirate-rev-order-maintenance = opening maintenance tunnels without a Security officer present is prohibited. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 107 (Trespassing).
pirate-rev-order-cryo = use of cryogenic treatment pods is prohibited. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-research = research requires Central Command approval for each technology, requested by fax. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-anomalies = all interaction with anomalies, including research and core collection, is prohibited. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 200 (Workplace Endangerment).
pirate-rev-order-salvage = salvage specialists and miners are prohibited from leaving the station. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-trade = sales to the trade station are prohibited. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-meat = preparation and consumption of meat dishes is prohibited. Chefs must prepare vegetarian dishes. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-botany = botanists may not use mutagens or fertilizers. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-radio = use of the common radio channel is prohibited except in emergencies. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 105 (Hooliganism).
pirate-rev-order-eng-modsuits = engineers, except the Chief Engineer, may not wear or use MODsuits without registration and a permit from Central Command. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 103 (Misuse of SCC Assets).
pirate-rev-order-eng-tools = personal tools are prohibited. Engineering issues tools only against a signature in a log that Security keeps. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 103 (Misuse of SCC Assets).
pirate-rev-order-eng-radsuits = all Engineering personnel, except the Chief Engineer, must wear radiation suits at all times while on duty. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 200 (Workplace Endangerment).
pirate-rev-order-atmos-canisters = gas canisters may not leave Atmospherics without a transfer form signed by Security. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 103 (Misuse of SCC Assets).
pirate-rev-order-med-paid = all medical treatment is paid. Medical sets the price, but the minimum price is 200 spesos. Before treatment, the patient pays to the medical budget. For treatment without payment, the patient is charged under article 106 (Petty Theft) and the doctor under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-med-sensors = all crew members must set their suit sensors to full tracking. Under this order, turning sensors down or off is an offence under article 105 (Hooliganism).
pirate-rev-order-med-certificates = all crew members must carry a health certificate signed by Medical. Security fines each crew member who works without a certificate.
pirate-rev-order-med-screening = each member of the medical staff must do a medical screening of at least 5 crew members and sign their health certificates. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-med-surgery = surgery is prohibited when neither the Chief Medical Officer nor a Security officer is present. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-chem-dispensers = use of chemical dispensers is paid. Chemists must write in a log the time when they enter and leave Chemistry, and pay 50 spesos to the Engineering budget for each minute in Chemistry. Security or the Chief Medical Officer checks the log against the airlock records from a LogProbe. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 106 (Petty Theft).
pirate-rev-order-service-paid-food = all food and drinks are paid. Each meal and each drink costs at least 50 spesos, paid to the Service budget. Under this order, food or drinks given for free are an offence under article 106 (Petty Theft).
pirate-rev-order-service-alcohol-log = the bartender must write the name of the buyer for each alcoholic drink in a log. Serving alcohol to a drunk person is prohibited. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 203 (Narcotics Offences).
pirate-rev-order-service-taste-test = a Security officer must taste all food before it is served. Under this order, serving food without a taste test is an offence under article 205 (Negligence).
pirate-rev-order-cargo-approval = each cargo order requires a written request, stamped by the Quartermaster and approved by Security or the Head of Personnel. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 103 (Misuse of SCC Assets).
pirate-rev-order-cargo-sales-tax = Cargo employees, except the Quartermaster, must pay a sales tax to the Security budget from their own accounts: 10% of the price of each shipment that they sell. Under this order, a violation is an offence under article 103 (Misuse of SCC Assets).

